  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/CB0150">Definition <span data-tag="CB0150">6.1.3.8</span>.</a>local!class of morphisms Let $\calX $ be a presentable $\infty $-category in which colimits are universal, and let $S$ be a class of morphisms in $\calX $. We will say that $S$ is <em>local</em> if it is stable under pullbacks and satisfies the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/C9D20A" data-tag="C9D20A">6.1.3.7</a>. </p>
